  "aiSummary": "This bill temporarily allows Buncombe County to use sales tax revenue for both school building projects and operating expenses (like teacher salaries and supplies) for two years, instead of only building projects. It also makes organizational changes to the School Capital Fund Commission that oversees these funds.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters argue this gives Buncombe County schools flexibility to address immediate operational needs alongside capital projects during a two-year period. This could help the county respond to budget pressures without waiting for the temporary measure to expire, while the Commission still advises on school facility priorities for both the county and Asheville city school systems.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents may be concerned that using sales tax revenue for operating expenses could become permanent practice, reducing funds available for long-term building investments and capital improvements. Some may also worry that allowing operating expense funding could reduce pressure on the county to adequately fund school operations through other budget sources.",
